  "candidates": [
    {
      "id": "REVIEW-TACTICAL-STACK-MASS-AGGREGATION-001",
      "severity": "P2 provisional; source-derived physical mass discrepancy with runtime impact unverified",
      "classification": "same first-failure family as checkpoint 059 ADLER stack-mass receiver and PL13 stack-mass connection, with current strategic, tactical and ammunition source trace",
      "detail": "The strategic connected-player view emits each personal inventory row with its independent positive quantity and catalog Item. The tactical projection installs one ItemProperties.weight from a unit catalog or instance/holder mass and separately installs TacticalItemQuantity. InventoryView iterates inventory entities and sums each property weight once without using quantity. Assuming an ordinary carried non-measured fungible stack with quantity above one and unit mass w, tactical aggregation contributes w while the strategic dry carried-mass calculation contributes quantity times w. The tactical motor, sprint-speed calculation and fatigue/work consumers use the tactical aggregate; no server or game was run.",
      "source_derived_example": "The authored arrow has 0.05 kg unit weight; a forester loadout specifies 28 arrows for the adult branch. For an otherwise successfully projected single 28-arrow personal row, with no food lot or fractional amount, no fireplace-rooted exclusion and no special weapon/holder appearance, the strategic dry mass is 1.40 kg for that row while the tactical aggregate is 0.05 kg, a 1.35 kg difference. The authored loadout supplies context, not proof that a particular deployed character, mission or row exists. Catalog JSON has no gameplay weapon design with catalog_id arrow, and connected holder appearance only handles scabbard and weapon_loop; unusual corrupt or alternate instance states remain outside this witness.",
      "ammunition_lifecycle": "A traced accepted ranged shot finds an arrow entity and decrements TacticalItemQuantity if another remains, or despawns it at zero. Since inventory_weight reads only unchanged ItemProperties.weight, the row contribution remains 0.05 kg as quantity falls from 28 to 27 in the conditional example; the source does not prove actual shot ordering, replication timing, database consequence completion or gameplay frequency.",
      "safeguards": "Zero quantity is rejected during tactical projection and quantity one naturally produces the same unit mass in the simple case. Weapon balance and weapon_weight also read ItemProperties.weight as an individual item property, so changing its meaning to stack total without tracing those consumers could introduce another error. Strategic mass separately handles food lots, fractional material, fireplace-rooted objects and contained water; their tactical transport and any reconciliation are not established by the simple-arrow witness.",
